<< /BS << /S /S /W 1>> /DA (/Helv 10 Tf 0 g) /F 4 /FT /Tx /Ff 4096 /MK << /BC [0.6 0.6 0.6]>> /P 122 0 R /Rect [73 561 539 654] /Subtype /Widget /T (Q9_answer) /Type /Annot /V (It defines a virtual base destructor for the base constructor. The programmer must make a derived destructor and when called it will activate both. If you do not have it when calling delete on a derived object through a base pointer then you will get undefined behavior. This could be something like memory leaks.) /AP << /N 469 0 R>> /M (D:20260731035610)>>
