<< /BS << /S /S /W 1>> /DA (/Helv 10 Tf 0 g) /F 4 /FT /Tx /Ff 4096 /MK << /BC [0.6 0.6 0.6]>> /P 122 0 R /Rect [73 426 539 519] /Subtype /Widget /T (Q10_answer) /Type /Annot /V (A function template will execute while keeping its variable type only for the duration of its use. The class will keep its function type across multiple calls as the function continues to get used. If you need to use the created item multiple times or for various different uses that would be in a class, you would use the class template. If you just need to make a specific variable version of a function and don't intend to use it again, you will be fine with the template function.) /AP << /N 470 0 R>> /M (D:20260731035610)>>
endobj
198 0 obj
<< /BS << /S /S /W 1>> /DA (/Helv 10 Tf 0 g) /F 4 /FT /Tx /Ff 4096 /MK << /BC [0.6 0.6 0.6]>> /P 122 0 R /Rect [73 291 539 384] /Subtype /Widget /T (Q11_answer) /Type /Annot /V (Clustering is when a large amount of slots get occupied next to one another in a hash table. When the load factor increases, these clusters increase in size, causing the program to have to search for longer to find an unoccupied slot. These longer search times lead to worse performance overall.) /AP << /N 471 0 R>> /M (D:20260731035610)>>
